==West Frisian==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/rik/|lang=fy}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|ofs|fy}} {{term|rike|rīke|lang=ofs}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fy}} {{recons|rīkijan||realm|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|fy}} {{recons|rīgiom||kingdom|lang=cel-pro}}, from {{recons|rīxs||king|lang=cel-pro}} (compare Irish {{term|rí|lang=ga}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|fy}} {{recons|h₃rḗǵs||king|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognates include Dutch {{term|rijk|lang=nl}}, obsolete English {{term|riche|lang=en}}, German {{term|Reich|lang=de}}, Danish {{term|rige|lang=da}}.

====Noun====
{{head|fy|noun|g=n}}

# [[realm]]

=====Derived terms=====

* [[keninkryk]]
* [[keizerryk]]

===Etymology 2===
From {{etyl|ofs|fy}} {{term|rike|rīke|lang=ofs}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|fy}} {{recons|rīkijaz||mighty|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{recons|rīks|lang=gem-pro}}, from {{etyl|cel-pro|fy}} {{recons|rīxs||king|lang=cel-pro}} (compare Irish {{term|rí|lang=ga}}), from {{etyl|ine-pro|fy}} {{recons|h₃rḗǵs||king|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognates include Dutch {{term|rijk|lang=nl}}, Low German {{term|rik|lang=nds}}, English {{term|rich|lang=en}}, German {{term|reich|lang=de}}, Danish {{term|rig|lang=da}}.

